1
00:00:02,160 --> 00:00:04,500
All right, they got water, orange juice...

2
00:00:04,870 --> 00:00:07,250
...and what looks like cider.

3
00:00:07,750 --> 00:00:08,790
Taste it.

4
00:00:13,930 --> 00:00:14,930
Yeah, it's fat.

5
00:00:15,180 --> 00:00:16,470
I drank fat!

6
00:00:18,220 --> 00:00:20,260
I know, I did that two minutes ago.

7
00:00:22,890 --> 00:00:23,930
Hey.

8
00:00:24,140 --> 00:00:25,600
Hey, Mr. Tux.

9
00:00:26,100 --> 00:00:28,440
- Why aren't you dressed?     - We have a half-hour.

10
00:00:28,690 --> 00:00:31,820
That was four minutes ago. We have to be out the door at 20 to 8.

11
00:00:32,070 --> 00:00:35,570
Relax, we'll be ready. It takes us two minutes to get dressed.

12
00:00:35,820 --> 00:00:37,990
I'd feel better if you got dressed now.

13
00:00:38,490 --> 00:00:39,910
- Okay.     - Okay.

14
00:00:42,660 --> 00:00:43,700
Hey!

15
00:00:43,870 --> 00:00:45,790
Oh, look at you, all sexy.

16
00:00:46,040 --> 00:00:47,080
Really?

17
00:00:50,920 --> 00:00:52,050
- Hi.     - Hi.

18
00:00:52,300 --> 00:00:57,180
- How come you didn't come over earlier?     - Because I'm a stupid, stupid man.

19
00:00:58,720 --> 00:01:00,470
Hey, Ross, want some cider?

20
00:01:00,720 --> 00:01:01,760
No.

21
00:01:03,140 --> 00:01:04,890
So you're pretty close, huh?

22
00:01:05,100 --> 00:01:06,940
Makeup's on. Hair's done.

23
00:01:07,190 --> 00:01:08,560
I just have to get dressed.

24
00:01:08,810 --> 00:01:11,610
And that takes, what? Just 6 or 7 minutes?

25
00:01:11,860 --> 00:01:14,230
Yeah. Once I figure out what I'm wearing.

26
00:01:17,030 --> 00:01:18,200
Glass of fat?

27
00:01:24,600 --> 00:01:29,100
# So no one told you life was gonna be this way #

28
00:01:29,670 --> 00:01:33,840
# Your job's a joke, you're broke, your love life's D.O.A. #

29
00:01:34,750 --> 00:01:38,560
# It's like you're always stuck in second gear #

30
00:01:39,020 --> 00:01:41,120
# When it hasn't been your day, #

31
00:01:41,120 --> 00:01:44,120
# your week, your month, or even your year #

32
00:01:44,120 --> 00:01:48,080
# but I'll be there for you #

33
00:01:48,080 --> 00:01:49,910
# When the rain starts to pour #

34
00:01:49,910 --> 00:01:53,030
# I'll be there for you #

35
00:01:53,030 --> 00:01:54,870
# Like I've been there before #

36
00:01:54,870 --> 00:01:57,880
# I'll be there for you #

37
00:01:57,880 --> 00:02:01,540
# 'Cause you're there for me too #

38
00:02:08,160 --> 00:02:11,040
What's the matter? You nervous about your speech?

39
00:02:11,290 --> 00:02:12,670
Nope.

40
00:02:14,210 --> 00:02:16,130
- You wanna hear it?     - Am I in it?

41
00:02:21,050 --> 00:02:23,970
After I thank everyone for donating to the museum...

42
00:02:24,220 --> 00:02:26,970
...I sing a song about the wonder that is Joey.

43
00:02:28,810 --> 00:02:29,850
- Hello.     - Hey.

44
00:02:31,230 --> 00:02:32,690
Hello! You look great!

45
00:02:32,940 --> 00:02:35,070
Thank you. I know, though.

46
00:02:36,690 --> 00:02:40,530
You see this? This is a person who is ready to go.

47
00:02:40,740 --> 00:02:41,950
Phoebe, you...

48
00:02:42,450 --> 00:02:43,570
You are my star.

49
00:02:43,910 --> 00:02:46,910
Aw. Well, you're my lucky penny.

50
00:02:49,870 --> 00:02:55,000
All right, I took the quiz, and it turns out I do put career before men.

51
00:02:57,760 --> 00:02:58,800
Get up.

52
00:02:59,220 --> 00:03:00,260
What?

53
00:03:00,680 --> 00:03:03,220
- You're in my seat.     - How is this your seat?

54
00:03:06,680 --> 00:03:07,930
I was sitting there.

55
00:03:08,100 --> 00:03:09,600
But then you left.

56
00:03:10,190 --> 00:03:12,730
Well, it's not like I went to Spain.

57
00:03:13,560 --> 00:03:15,900
I went to the bathroom. You knew I'd be back.

58
00:03:16,110 --> 00:03:17,940
What's the big deal? Sit somewhere else!

59
00:03:18,110 --> 00:03:21,700
The "big deal" is, I was sitting there last! So...

60
00:03:21,950 --> 00:03:23,240
...it's my seat.

61
00:03:23,780 --> 00:03:27,950
Well, actually, the last place you were sitting was in there, so...

62
00:03:28,450 --> 00:03:31,000
You guys, you know what? It doesn't matter.

63
00:03:31,250 --> 00:03:35,790
You both have to go get dressed before the big vein in my head pops.

64
00:03:36,040 --> 00:03:38,800
I just have to do one thing. It's not a big deal.

65
00:03:39,090 --> 00:03:40,210
Get up!

66
00:03:42,010 --> 00:03:43,050
- Hi.     - Hey.

67
00:03:43,260 --> 00:03:45,510
Ooh. Phoebe, you look great!

68
00:03:46,140 --> 00:03:47,970
All right already.

69
00:03:48,890 --> 00:03:50,770
Ooh. Are you gonna do magic?

70
00:03:53,270 --> 00:03:55,060
That's funny. Change.

71
00:03:55,270 --> 00:03:57,150
- Hang on, I just got in.     - I don't care.

72
00:03:57,440 --> 00:03:59,230
It starts at 8. We can't be late.

73
00:03:59,480 --> 00:04:02,320
"He could not, would not, want to wait."

74
00:04:03,070 --> 00:04:05,820
Our table is down in front. My boss will be there.

75
00:04:06,070 --> 00:04:08,450
Everyone will see if we arrive after it starts.

76
00:04:08,660 --> 00:04:10,660
Has somebody been drinking my fat?

77
00:04:12,250 --> 00:04:16,000
Does this look like something a paleontologist's girlfriend would wear?

78
00:04:16,250 --> 00:04:18,840
I don't know. You might be the first one.

79
00:04:20,130 --> 00:04:22,340
- Rach, did you check the machine?     - No.

80
00:04:22,760 --> 00:04:26,680
Wait. This is the outfit that makes my calves look fat. Never mind.

81
00:04:30,560 --> 00:04:33,430
Well, Joey, I wrote a little song today.

82
00:04:33,850 --> 00:04:35,190
It's called, "Get up!"

83
00:04:36,440 --> 00:04:39,110
All right. You can have the chair.

84
00:04:39,320 --> 00:04:42,530
- Really?     - Oh, my. Would you look at that?

85
00:04:46,660 --> 00:04:48,160
I'm coming over.

86
00:04:48,370 --> 00:04:50,990
What if I'm already there when you play this message?

87
00:04:51,200 --> 00:04:53,120
Is that too spooky?

88
00:04:55,160 --> 00:04:57,670
Hi, Rach, are you there? It's me. Pick up.

89
00:04:58,130 --> 00:04:59,880
Rachel? Rach?

90
00:05:00,380 --> 00:05:01,630
What?

91
00:05:03,130 --> 00:05:04,170
Never mind.

92
00:05:06,550 --> 00:05:09,050
Monica, it's Richard. Call me.

93
00:05:12,720 --> 00:05:14,220
Is that message old or new?

94
00:05:15,730 --> 00:05:17,350
Old or new? Old or new?

95
00:05:17,600 --> 00:05:20,400
It's definitely old. Didn't you hear the double beep?

96
00:05:20,690 --> 00:05:23,070
What if it's new? We agreed not to talk.

97
00:05:23,230 --> 00:05:26,070
It could be important. Shouldn't I call him back?

98
00:05:26,320 --> 00:05:28,700
Honey, you did call him back. It's old.

99
00:05:28,910 --> 00:05:30,990
Yeah, see, Mon, listen. Listen.

100
00:05:31,200 --> 00:05:33,330
When Carol and I broke up...

101
00:05:33,580 --> 00:05:36,620
...I went through the same thing. You know what I did?

102
00:05:36,830 --> 00:05:38,830
I got dressed.

103
00:05:41,420 --> 00:05:44,340
Really, really quickly, okay? Okay?

104
00:05:44,550 --> 00:05:46,590
There we go. There we go.

105
00:05:47,340 --> 00:05:49,760
You know what? Don't get up. Just sit there.

106
00:05:50,050 --> 00:05:53,100
I just hope you don't mind my hand right here.

107
00:05:54,390 --> 00:05:57,730
Not touching. Can't get mad! Not touching. Can't get mad!

108
00:05:57,940 --> 00:06:00,100
Not touching. Can't get mad!

109
00:06:00,360 --> 00:06:02,730
Oh! Oh, my God!

110
00:06:03,190 --> 00:06:04,610
You rotten boys!

111
00:06:05,780 --> 00:06:08,030
- Sorry, Phoebe.     - What am I gonna do?

112
00:06:08,280 --> 00:06:10,110
Don't rub it! What gets out hummus?

113
00:06:10,370 --> 00:06:12,030
What gets out hummus?

114
00:06:12,530 --> 00:06:14,580
Monica! What gets out hummus?

115
00:06:15,620 --> 00:06:18,960
If it is a new message, what is he calling to say?

116
00:06:19,790 --> 00:06:22,040
Okay, thanks. Yeah, I'll try that.

117
00:06:23,630 --> 00:06:25,800
Maybe he called to say you're obsessive and crazy?

118
00:06:26,090 --> 00:06:28,300
- So should I call him back?     - No!

119
00:06:29,680 --> 00:06:30,720
No!

120
00:06:32,800 --> 00:06:35,810
- Fine, we'll both sit in the chair.     - Fine with me.

121
00:06:39,690 --> 00:06:42,060
I am so comfortable.

122
00:06:43,310 --> 00:06:44,310
Me too.

123
00:06:44,650 --> 00:06:48,190
In fact, I think I might be a little too comfortable.

124
00:06:52,320 --> 00:06:55,910
Okay, we have 19 minutes. I want you to go and change.

125
00:06:56,160 --> 00:07:00,330
When you come back, Joey will go change, and he'll have vacated the chair.

126
00:07:00,750 --> 00:07:01,830
- Okay.     - All right.

127
00:07:02,080 --> 00:07:03,630
Fine. I'm going.

128
00:07:03,840 --> 00:07:07,420
When I get back, it's Chair City. And I'm the guy...

129
00:07:07,630 --> 00:07:09,340
...who's sitting in a chair!

130
00:07:11,470 --> 00:07:12,800
Is this a little too...?

131
00:07:13,010 --> 00:07:15,010
Pheebs? What happened?

132
00:07:15,260 --> 00:07:16,510
I got the hummus.

133
00:07:16,810 --> 00:07:20,770
Oh, honey, we'll find you something. You wanna wear my black jacket?

134
00:07:20,980 --> 00:07:23,190
- It won't go with this dress.     - You're right.

135
00:07:23,440 --> 00:07:27,820
- Well, let's just get you out of that.     - No, no, no. Not out of that.

136
00:07:28,030 --> 00:07:30,940
- Not out of clothes.     - Can Phoebe borrow your green dress?

137
00:07:31,110 --> 00:07:32,150
I called him.

138
00:07:33,610 --> 00:07:36,740
Yes. I got his machine and I left a message.

139
00:07:36,990 --> 00:07:38,450
But it's okay. It's okay...

140
00:07:38,700 --> 00:07:41,870
...because it was, like, a casual, breezy message.

141
00:07:42,120 --> 00:07:43,170
It was breezy.

142
00:07:44,040 --> 00:07:45,960
Oh, God, what if it wasn't breezy?

143
00:07:46,170 --> 00:07:50,550
How could it not be breezy? No, because you're in such a breezy place.

144
00:07:51,300 --> 00:07:55,510
I got it. I'll play my message, and you guys tell me if it's breezy enough.

145
00:07:55,720 --> 00:07:57,800
But how you gonna do that?

146
00:07:58,390 --> 00:08:00,890
I know the code to his answering machine.

147
00:08:01,140 --> 00:08:03,690
Okay, Mon, I really don't think this is the...

148
00:08:03,900 --> 00:08:06,650
Okay, you're dialing. You are dialing.

149
00:08:16,820 --> 00:08:19,530
Hi, this is Richard. Please leave a message at the tone.

150
00:08:21,870 --> 00:08:23,580
You have two new messages.

151
00:08:24,040 --> 00:08:25,420
What a cool job.

152
00:08:25,710 --> 00:08:27,670
"You have two new messages."

153
00:08:29,550 --> 00:08:31,840
Please pass the pie.

154
00:08:34,180 --> 00:08:36,800
Hi, it's Monica. I'm just checking in.

155
00:08:37,010 --> 00:08:40,260
I got a message and didn't know if it was old or new...

156
00:08:40,520 --> 00:08:42,520
...so I'm just checking.

157
00:08:42,730 --> 00:08:44,350
So let me know.

158
00:08:44,600 --> 00:08:45,940
Or don't. Whatever.

159
00:08:46,230 --> 00:08:47,770
I'm breezy!

160
00:08:49,190 --> 00:08:52,610
You can't say you're "breezy." That negates the "breezy."

161
00:08:54,900 --> 00:08:57,860
Hola. It's me. Yesterday was really fun.

162
00:08:58,570 --> 00:09:00,830
Call me about this weekend, okay?

163
00:09:04,120 --> 00:09:05,750
Now, she sounded breezy.

164
00:09:09,460 --> 00:09:13,130
He's seeing someone. I can't believe he's seeing someone.

165
00:09:13,380 --> 00:09:15,970
- You don't know that.     - Well, whose voice was that?

166
00:09:16,130 --> 00:09:19,140
Maybe it was his sister's. Maybe it was his daughter's.

167
00:09:20,510 --> 00:09:23,810
Michelle. Of course! Did it sound like Michelle?

168
00:09:24,480 --> 00:09:28,480
Oh, great. It's starting to rain. That'll make it easier to get a cab.

169
00:09:29,480 --> 00:09:30,480
It was Michelle.

170
00:09:30,690 --> 00:09:32,400
It was definitely Michelle.

171
00:09:32,650 --> 00:09:36,820
Try Monica's green dress. If it doesn't fit, wear my gray silk one.

172
00:09:37,110 --> 00:09:39,660
- Unless I wear it.     - You don't know what you're wearing?

173
00:09:39,870 --> 00:09:42,490
I'm just trying to look nice for your big night.

174
00:09:42,700 --> 00:09:45,370
Yeah, which we have to leave for in 12 minutes.

175
00:09:45,660 --> 00:09:48,370
Come on, I'll just pick something out for you.

176
00:09:48,670 --> 00:09:50,880
You'll notice that I'm fully dressed.

177
00:09:51,170 --> 00:09:54,500
I, in turn, have noticed that you are not.

178
00:09:54,760 --> 00:09:59,550
So in the words of A.A. Milne, "Get out of my chair, dill-hole."

179
00:10:02,010 --> 00:10:03,390
Okay.

180
00:10:11,060 --> 00:10:13,690
- What are you doing?     - You said to give you the chair.

181
00:10:13,940 --> 00:10:16,030
You didn't say anything about cushions.

182
00:10:16,190 --> 00:10:17,900
They're the essence of the chair!

183
00:10:18,200 --> 00:10:20,780
That's right! I'm taking the essence.

184
00:10:21,870 --> 00:10:23,700
Oh, he'll be back.

185
00:10:23,910 --> 00:10:26,370
Oh, there's nobody in the room.

186
00:10:27,040 --> 00:10:30,670
- I'm sorry, I thought it looked pretty.     - That was a Halloween costume.

187
00:10:30,880 --> 00:10:34,210
Unless you would like me to go as Little Bo Peep.

188
00:10:34,670 --> 00:10:37,380
I didn't recognize it without that inflatable sheep.

189
00:10:37,670 --> 00:10:41,430
Yeah, which, by the way, Chandler, I would like back one of these days.

190
00:10:44,060 --> 00:10:46,720
Rach, good! Listen, isn't this perfect for me?

191
00:10:46,930 --> 00:10:49,270
Oh, it's perfect! But not for tonight.

192
00:10:49,560 --> 00:10:52,900
Of course not for tonight. Hi. I'm going to a benefit.

193
00:10:53,110 --> 00:10:55,230
Not for tonight? What are you doing?

194
00:10:55,440 --> 00:10:58,780
No, I'm sorry. We didn't mean it. I love you. Breathe.

195
00:11:00,200 --> 00:11:03,200
We used them as pillows when we went camping.

196
00:11:03,410 --> 00:11:04,410
What?

197
00:11:05,410 --> 00:11:06,580
The sheep.

198
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:10,790
Hey, what you do on your own time...

199
00:11:14,460 --> 00:11:16,920
Where's my underwear?

200
00:11:17,090 --> 00:11:20,590
- Come on, you took his underwear?     - He took my essence!

201
00:11:20,800 --> 00:11:25,640
Okay, hold on. Why can't you just wear the underwear you're wearing now?

202
00:11:25,930 --> 00:11:28,520
Because I'm not wearing any underwear now.

203
00:11:29,730 --> 00:11:32,100
Then why do you have to wear underwear tonight?

204
00:11:32,350 --> 00:11:34,100
It's a rented tux, okay?

205
00:11:34,360 --> 00:11:37,650
I'm not gonna go "commando" in another man's fatigues.

206
00:11:39,990 --> 00:11:43,450
Then somebody's gonna have to give somebody back his cushions.

207
00:11:44,280 --> 00:11:48,450
Okay. You hide my clothes. I'm gonna do the exact opposite to you.

208
00:11:50,790 --> 00:11:53,870
What, are you gonna show me my clothes?

209
00:11:54,130 --> 00:11:55,540
Hey, opposite...

210
00:11:56,540 --> 00:11:57,790
...is opposite.

211
00:11:59,630 --> 00:12:01,260
He's got nothing!

212
00:12:02,130 --> 00:12:03,680
Okay, I'm ready.

213
00:12:08,970 --> 00:12:12,140
Rachel didn't have anything I liked but this ribbon.

214
00:12:12,350 --> 00:12:14,810
I thought, all right, I'll be political.

215
00:12:16,560 --> 00:12:19,650
- What are you supporting?     - Christmas.

216
00:12:21,150 --> 00:12:26,160
Hey, that's okay with me. Two down, and I have exactly 12 minutes...

217
00:12:26,660 --> 00:12:27,660
What?

218
00:12:28,700 --> 00:12:31,290
My watch stopped. My watch. Okay, see...

219
00:12:31,500 --> 00:12:34,330
...the dinosaur tail isn't going around anymore.

220
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:37,580
What time is it? It's 7:33. I have 7 minutes.

221
00:12:37,840 --> 00:12:39,000
I have seven minutes!

222
00:12:39,170 --> 00:12:42,170
Which shoes should I wear? The black or the purple?

223
00:12:42,510 --> 00:12:44,880
- Just pick one, okay?     - Oh, okay, okay. The black.

224
00:12:45,090 --> 00:12:47,390
Do you have black with little strappies?

225
00:12:47,680 --> 00:12:51,680
Yeah, but those go better with pants. Maybe I should wear pants.

226
00:12:52,180 --> 00:12:56,810
Yeah, pants! What an idea! Or better yet, go without pants.

227
00:12:57,020 --> 00:13:00,110
I don't know what you're doing but just get in there...

228
00:13:00,360 --> 00:13:02,860
...and pick out any shoes that fit your feet.

229
00:13:03,030 --> 00:13:06,530
I don't care if they match. I don't care if they make...

230
00:13:06,740 --> 00:13:11,370
...your ankles or your knees or your earlobes look fat. Just do it!

231
00:13:11,580 --> 00:13:14,250
Go in there, pick something out so we can go.

232
00:13:17,040 --> 00:13:19,540
- All right.     - Thank you.

233
00:13:20,420 --> 00:13:24,090
I've got to call Michelle to see if that was her voice.

234
00:13:24,340 --> 00:13:26,220
It was. It was her voice.

235
00:13:26,470 --> 00:13:29,550
Monica, I think you've gone over to the bad place.

236
00:13:33,560 --> 00:13:35,390
Hola.

237
00:13:35,730 --> 00:13:38,060
Hello? Hello?

238
00:13:39,400 --> 00:13:42,480
- Okay. That was her, right?     - Definitely. Yeah.

239
00:13:42,730 --> 00:13:44,570
So there you go. Whew!

240
00:13:44,740 --> 00:13:48,070
We're out of the woods. I think I'll get dressed now.

241
00:13:49,620 --> 00:13:51,410
- I'll get it.     - Okay.

242
00:13:52,660 --> 00:13:54,120
Hi, Monica and Rachel's.

243
00:13:54,620 --> 00:13:57,660
Yeah, just a second. Can I ask who's calling?

244
00:13:57,960 --> 00:13:59,250
Ooh! It's Michelle! Ooh!

245
00:14:01,460 --> 00:14:05,420
She must have that "caller I.D." thing. You should get that.

246
00:14:08,430 --> 00:14:09,470
Michelle?

247
00:14:09,930 --> 00:14:13,930
Yeah, that was me. I dialed your number by mistake.

248
00:14:14,180 --> 00:14:15,310
Just try to be...

249
00:14:17,310 --> 00:14:18,770
You're so sweet.

250
00:14:19,440 --> 00:14:21,480
Yeah, we were a great couple.

251
00:14:21,810 --> 00:14:23,690
I know, I really miss him.

252
00:14:24,280 --> 00:14:26,900
